{{!
    @template tiny_sheetmusic/midihelp

    What MIDI import can and cannot do.

    A MIDI import is a guess and never a transcription, and RELATIONS.md section B3 rule 2
    makes saying so a contract rather than a courtesy. The wording is the copy approved in
    P0-FINDINGS-T3 section B5, which was written against measured behaviour of the quantiser.

    Collapsed by default because it is long and most authors are typing ABC rather than
    importing anything; tiny_sheetmusic/ui opens it the moment a MIDI file is chosen.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-region="midihelp" - the disclosure the import path opens.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * none

    Example context (json):
    {
    }
}}
<details class="tiny_sheetmusic-midihelp" data-region="midihelp">
    <summary>{{#str}}midihelpsummary, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</summary>
    <div class="tiny_sheetmusic-midihelp-body">
        <p>{{#str}}midihelpintro, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</p>

        <h6>{{#str}}midihelpreliable, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</h6>
        <ul>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpreliable1, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpreliable2, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpreliable3, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
        </ul>

        <h6>{{#str}}midihelpfix, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</h6>
        <ul>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpfix1, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpfix2, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpfix3, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpfix4, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
            <li>{{#str}}midihelpfix5, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</li>
        </ul>

        <h6>{{#str}}midihelpnometre, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</h6>
        <p>{{#str}}midihelpnometrebody, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</p>

        <h6>{{#str}}midihelpgrid, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</h6>
        <p>{{#str}}midihelpgridbody, tiny_sheetmusic{{/str}}</p>
    </div>
</details>
